{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776790583,"nonce":"IEuYrqDPIIQhUIP/1t1q9ryQr08=","title":"Report suspended:provider-overload instead of max-resumes when provider is overloaded","message":"## Problem\n\nWhen sessions fail due to provider rate limits / \"high demand\" errors, they report `suspended:max-resumes` which is misleading. The agent isn't incapable - the provider is overloaded.\n\n## Example\n\njessica-ng sessions `f41708f` and `8d71d2d` both failed with:\n```\nerror: Reconnecting... 5/5 (We're currently experiencing high demand, which may cause temporary errors.)\n```\n\nBoth ended up as `suspended:max-resumes` when they should be `suspended:provider-overload`.\n\n## Solution\n\n1. **Detect provider overload:** In `HeadlessAgentBase._is_transient_error()`, distinguish:\n   - Transient (retry): 429, 500-504, \"rate limit\", \"high demand\", \"overloaded\"\n   - After max retries exhausted: emit `AgentEventType.PROVIDER_OVERLOAD` (new type)\n\n2. **New status:** `suspended:provider-overload` in SessionRunner when overload is detected\n\n3. **Backoff retry:** Instead of immediate max-resumes suspension, apply exponential backoff between resume attempts for overload (30s, 60s, 120s, 240s)\n\n## Tests\n\n- tests/test_session_runner.py::test_provider_overload_status_reported\n- tests/test_codex_agent.py::test_high_demand_detected_as_overload\n- tests/test_session_runner.py::test_backoff_on_provider_overload\n\n## Files\n\n- core/protocols.py (add AgentEventType.PROVIDER_OVERLOAD)\n- adapters/agents/base.py (detect overload after transient retries exhausted)\n- adapters/agents/codex.py (emit PROVIDER_OVERLOAD on 5/5 reconnect failure)\n- core/session.py (handle PROVIDER_OVERLOAD, set new status, apply backoff)\n- core/state.py (add suspended:provider-overload status)\n\n## Related\n\n- docs/codex-agent-plan.md \"Future Enhancements: Exponential backoff on provider overload\"\n\nREQ: REQ-032 or new REQ","files":null}]}